WEBVTT

00:43.210 --> 00:48.424
CHAPTER 39: USE A BIT OF SENSE
AND FIGURE IT OUT YOURSELF

00:48.883 --> 00:51.677
Mr. Ga! Wait a minute.

00:51.761 --> 00:53.429
Sir! I have something to say!

00:53.512 --> 00:55.222
Just a moment. Wait.

00:55.306 --> 00:56.891
Just a second.

01:01.145 --> 01:02.146
Just a moment.

01:05.900 --> 01:06.984
What is it?

01:16.118 --> 01:17.161
I…

01:23.083 --> 01:24.126
I…

01:28.214 --> 01:30.925
I'm struggling with the after-school math.

01:37.348 --> 01:38.182
What?

01:40.059 --> 01:40.893
You know,

01:41.852 --> 01:43.437
I…

01:45.606 --> 01:47.983
I keep skipping the homework,

01:48.067 --> 01:51.237
and I feel like I'm holding
the other girls back.

01:52.488 --> 01:54.448
It's weighing on my heart.

01:54.532 --> 01:56.492
I feel so guilty, sir.

02:00.287 --> 02:02.581
So you get no desire at all to learn more?

02:03.749 --> 02:05.793
What happened to the promise
you made ten years ago?

02:06.418 --> 02:08.045
You talked so big back then.

02:09.839 --> 02:10.714
Sorry?

02:11.465 --> 02:12.508
I'm talking about you.

02:13.217 --> 02:14.260
Eui-ju.

02:17.847 --> 02:19.557
I what?

02:20.558 --> 02:23.644
I really believed
you would be good at math.

02:27.940 --> 02:28.941
You're saying

02:29.775 --> 02:31.986
I made a promise to you?

02:32.069 --> 02:33.195
What promise?

02:34.655 --> 02:35.698
Forget it.

02:37.366 --> 02:38.450
What?

02:38.534 --> 02:39.952
Mr. Ga, wait.

02:40.035 --> 02:40.953
EPISODE 13

02:41.036 --> 02:43.706
Tell me what promise I made.

02:43.789 --> 02:44.915
Mr. Ga!

02:46.917 --> 02:48.377
Did you tidy the classroom?

02:50.212 --> 02:51.046
Oh, right.

02:54.758 --> 02:55.885
Goodbye.

03:15.195 --> 03:16.113
Promise?

03:17.156 --> 03:20.034
I can't do it.

03:20.117 --> 03:22.119
I just can't.

03:22.202 --> 03:23.871
Then write him a letter.

03:24.455 --> 03:25.331
A letter?

03:25.414 --> 03:26.665
Sure, you're a writer.

03:26.749 --> 03:27.958
Use your words to shoot your shot.

03:30.294 --> 03:31.211
Shoot my shot?

03:36.050 --> 03:39.261
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 9

03:44.016 --> 03:45.017
I'm here.

03:47.811 --> 03:51.482
Why didn't I think of this before?

03:52.775 --> 03:56.236
All I had to do was tell him how I felt
through my work.

03:56.862 --> 03:58.238
Dig in. I know you're hungry.

03:58.322 --> 03:59.531
Thanks.

04:04.370 --> 04:05.579
Are you really choosing me,

04:06.080 --> 04:08.958
or are you just running away from Tae-ha?

04:09.750 --> 04:12.044
-Is there a difference?
-There's a huge difference!

04:15.547 --> 04:17.007
I don't want to be your refuge.

04:18.384 --> 04:20.219
It's just hard thinking about Tae-ha.

04:21.637 --> 04:23.931
It's easier, being around you.

04:24.556 --> 04:25.849
Easier?

04:26.517 --> 04:27.559
So that's what I am to you.

04:29.228 --> 04:30.354
That's kind of harsh.

04:32.231 --> 04:34.441
Sorry for being so selfish.

04:34.525 --> 04:36.026
It's fine, since I'm selfish myself.

04:37.027 --> 04:39.279
If I'm by your side when you're confused,

04:39.363 --> 04:40.948
you might end up choosing me.

04:41.031 --> 04:44.743
IN THAT MOMENT,
YOON DECIDED TO SHOOT HIS SHOT

04:45.953 --> 04:47.454
Si-on, I like you.

04:47.538 --> 04:54.044
SI-ON, I LIKE YOU

04:54.837 --> 04:56.088
To tell the truth,

04:57.339 --> 04:59.425
I've liked you for a long time.

04:59.508 --> 05:00.592
Since high school.

05:04.138 --> 05:06.015
If I didn't tell you today,

05:06.098 --> 05:07.808
I think I'd regret it
for the rest of my life.

05:17.317 --> 05:18.861
How can you not know how I feel?

05:18.944 --> 05:20.029
Do I have to spell it out?

05:20.112 --> 05:22.531
Can't you use a bit of sense
and figure it out yourself?

05:26.243 --> 05:27.286
I like you.

05:27.369 --> 05:29.329
Every time you look at me,

05:30.122 --> 05:32.541
I feel like my heart's going to explode.

05:33.292 --> 05:34.835
When you so much as pass me by,

05:35.461 --> 05:36.712
my heart flutters.

05:37.921 --> 05:39.173
Even now.

05:39.256 --> 05:41.675
Even when you picked on me
and acted all mean.

05:41.759 --> 05:43.927
Even when you humiliated me
for being terrible at math.

05:45.220 --> 05:47.139
I never hated you.

05:47.681 --> 05:49.725
I like you. I like you, okay?

05:49.808 --> 05:51.810
I really like you, Si-on!

05:56.023 --> 05:57.066
I like you.

06:09.745 --> 06:10.871
So,

06:10.954 --> 06:12.664
you didn't write the letter?

06:12.748 --> 06:13.874
Well…

06:13.957 --> 06:15.959
I'll do it some other time.

06:16.043 --> 06:17.836
Jeez. Some other time when?

06:18.921 --> 06:21.131
Even if I confess my feelings,

06:21.757 --> 06:23.092
will anything change?

06:23.759 --> 06:27.262
Let's say I work up the courage
to tell him I like him.

06:27.346 --> 06:30.432
What then?
It's not like he's going to reciprocate.

06:31.809 --> 06:33.685
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

06:33.769 --> 06:35.062
Good morning.

06:40.192 --> 06:42.486
Go talk to him.

06:42.569 --> 06:43.862
Go.

06:45.114 --> 06:46.532
Mr. Ga.

06:46.615 --> 06:48.158
Well…

06:48.242 --> 06:50.244
I uploaded a new episode yesterday.

06:50.327 --> 06:52.746
Did you get a chance to see it?

06:52.830 --> 06:54.331
What did you think?

06:56.416 --> 06:58.710
It was weird how Yoon changed so much.

06:59.503 --> 07:01.839
Why would he say that?
That came out of nowhere.

07:07.928 --> 07:09.054
What's wrong?

07:10.013 --> 07:11.849
Why? What did he say?

07:11.932 --> 07:12.850
It was nothing.

07:15.144 --> 07:16.228
-Let's just go.
-Huh?

07:18.313 --> 07:20.691
-Good morning.
-Good morning.

07:21.900 --> 07:23.527
Did you all bring your assignments?

07:23.610 --> 07:24.444
-Yes.
-Yes.

07:24.528 --> 07:26.238
Hand them in now. Don't do them in class.

07:26.321 --> 07:27.281
Pass them forward.

07:27.364 --> 07:28.240
-Okay.
-Okay.

07:29.533 --> 07:30.659
-Hang on.
-Just a sec.

07:42.671 --> 07:43.672
Did anyone not do it?

07:47.009 --> 07:47.843
Me, sir.

07:50.012 --> 07:51.430
Stand up, Eui-ju.

07:55.934 --> 07:57.186
Why didn't you do it?

07:57.936 --> 07:59.229
I forgot, sir.

08:00.230 --> 08:01.190
Forgot?

08:01.815 --> 08:02.983
What happened to your priorities?

08:04.151 --> 08:07.029
Shouldn't your top priorities
be studying and working on homework?

08:07.112 --> 08:08.280
Am I wrong?

08:09.990 --> 08:11.408
Are you going to keep this up?

08:13.076 --> 08:14.119
No, sir.

08:14.203 --> 08:17.080
I want you to do the original assignment
plus some advanced problems by tomorrow.

08:18.999 --> 08:20.042
Yes, sir.

08:20.125 --> 08:21.126
Sit down.

08:27.007 --> 08:28.091
All right, turn to page 99.

08:28.175 --> 08:30.260
Did you do something wrong?

08:30.344 --> 08:32.054
Why is he so harsh on you?

08:32.930 --> 08:34.264
I don't know.

08:34.348 --> 08:35.474
I'm screwed.

08:40.270 --> 08:41.563
Why is he so uptight?

08:41.647 --> 08:43.023
CHAPTER 40:
YOU THINK YOU COULD HIDE IT?

08:43.106 --> 08:44.691
That pop quiz we took in math.

08:44.775 --> 08:46.443
Mr. Ga said no half marks.

08:47.486 --> 08:48.820
He has no compassion.

08:49.446 --> 08:50.697
It's like he's AI.

08:52.074 --> 08:54.076
Isn't he just following the rules?

08:54.993 --> 08:56.495
That might actually be more fair.

08:57.162 --> 08:59.039
What are you talking about?

08:59.122 --> 09:01.458
So what if he's got a pretty face?

09:01.541 --> 09:03.001
Exactly.

09:03.085 --> 09:04.294
That's what's even more annoying.

09:04.378 --> 09:06.672
He's so handsome like a prince charming,

09:07.297 --> 09:08.674
but his personality sucks.

09:08.757 --> 09:10.509
It really ruins the fantasy.

09:10.592 --> 09:13.053
His personality isn't that bad.

09:13.136 --> 09:14.137
He's just a bit spiky.

09:20.018 --> 09:21.687
What's up with you today?

09:21.770 --> 09:23.689
You used to talk crap about him
all the time.

09:24.564 --> 09:26.108
Why are you taking his side?

09:28.610 --> 09:30.779
Me? When did I do that?

09:34.992 --> 09:35.826
By any chance,

09:36.952 --> 09:38.078
do you have a crush on him?

09:41.707 --> 09:42.749
Hey.

09:43.250 --> 09:44.876
Watch what you say.

09:45.460 --> 09:46.336
She's not crazy.

09:47.546 --> 09:48.505
Right.

09:49.089 --> 09:50.340
I took it too far.

09:50.841 --> 09:52.384
You crossed the line.

09:52.467 --> 09:53.802
Sorry. My bad.

09:53.885 --> 09:55.429
Let's go. See you later, Eui-ju.

09:59.599 --> 10:01.143
You idiot.

10:01.226 --> 10:04.604
They say you can't hide
love and a cough, kiddo.

10:04.688 --> 10:06.982
Have I been found out?
Do you think they caught on?

10:08.525 --> 10:09.735
I'd better be careful.

10:12.529 --> 10:14.031
Isn't the school in that web novel

10:14.114 --> 10:15.198
just like ours?

10:15.282 --> 10:17.743
-You think?
-The characters are like our teachers.

10:17.826 --> 10:20.787
The ice hockey player Tae-ha is Mr. Jung,
and the rich returning student is Mr. Noh.

10:21.413 --> 10:22.748
Hey, check this out.

10:23.373 --> 10:27.085
"He always wears a beige cardigan
and an old brown leather-band watch."

10:27.169 --> 10:29.004
That's Mr. Yoon.

10:29.087 --> 10:30.797
You're right. I saw him earlier.

10:30.881 --> 10:32.841
He was wearing that cardigan again.

10:32.924 --> 10:34.009
I'm telling you I'm right.

10:34.092 --> 10:36.011
The other one is definitely Mr. Ga.

10:36.094 --> 10:38.138
The other day in class,

10:38.221 --> 10:40.599
I saw how he always crooks his pinky
when he adjusts his glasses.

10:40.682 --> 10:42.225
-Really?
-Five times out of five.

10:42.309 --> 10:43.310
That's just like Si-on.

10:43.894 --> 10:45.562
I'm shipping Si-on with Yoon.

10:45.645 --> 10:47.439
I'm all for Tae-ha and Yoon.

10:47.522 --> 10:48.357
WE WERE FRIENDS

10:48.440 --> 10:49.274
Ju Si-on?

10:49.358 --> 10:50.817
-Kang Tae-ha?
-Look.

10:51.401 --> 10:52.611
Choi Yoon?

10:53.111 --> 10:54.738
…AND TURNS HIS WATCH TO LOOK AT IT

11:04.664 --> 11:06.666
"Si-on said,

11:06.750 --> 11:08.794
-'When a star is born…'"
-When a star is born,

11:08.877 --> 11:10.712
countless clouds of dust
surround it so densely

11:10.796 --> 11:11.963
you can't even see an inch ahead.

11:12.047 --> 11:13.423
That's why people say…

11:13.507 --> 11:16.927
"That's why people say
stars are born out of chaos."

11:17.010 --> 11:20.347
This problem might seem complicated,
but you'll find that it's actually simple.

11:20.972 --> 11:22.516
In fact, no math problem

11:23.392 --> 11:24.976
can ever be as complicated as life.

11:26.478 --> 11:29.189
Those are all things Mr. Ga said.

11:30.148 --> 11:31.733
Does this mean the writer

11:32.651 --> 11:34.194
is in our class?

11:35.195 --> 11:36.363
And in after-school math?

11:37.864 --> 11:39.658
Put some heart into it, okay?
Hey, Ms. Eui-ju.

11:39.741 --> 11:40.826
Put some heart into it.

11:40.909 --> 11:43.120
Your drawings must suck
for her to be like this, girl.

11:43.203 --> 11:45.038
-Let me tell you about drawing…
-Unbelievable.

11:45.872 --> 11:47.416
What do you know about drawing?

11:47.499 --> 11:49.501
-Okay, Picasso.
-Give me a break.

11:49.584 --> 11:50.919
Okay.

11:51.002 --> 11:53.004
Eui-ju is the only one who fits the bill.

11:57.467 --> 11:59.719
-This is great.
-Jenny, what are you reading?

12:00.387 --> 12:02.347
Fifty Shades of Mr. CEO.

12:03.432 --> 12:06.143
The male lead
has finally confessed his feelings.

12:06.226 --> 12:07.227
No way! How did he do it?

12:08.728 --> 12:09.771
Like this.

12:09.855 --> 12:10.897
And then.

12:12.524 --> 12:14.568
"You know I can't live without you."

12:15.652 --> 12:16.778
"How could you resign?"

12:19.114 --> 12:22.993
According to the comments,
she goes to his place in the next episode.

12:23.076 --> 12:25.162
I guess he's going to pretend to be sick.

12:25.245 --> 12:26.955
It's such a cliché.

12:27.956 --> 12:31.585
But even though it's clichéd,
people still go crazy for it.

12:31.668 --> 12:34.171
This is so cringe, but why is it so good?

12:34.254 --> 12:38.758
Romance novels are
such a classic for a reason!

12:38.842 --> 12:39.885
You're so right.

12:39.968 --> 12:43.680
Works of mega-hit writers
are all quite similar, right?

12:43.763 --> 12:45.265
Why? Is it not going well?

12:45.348 --> 12:46.641
You said you were done.

12:46.725 --> 12:48.727
You'll keep it a secret
even if you hit the big time?

12:48.810 --> 12:49.853
The big time?

12:51.396 --> 12:54.858
-You'll be the first one I tell.
-That's right.

12:57.861 --> 12:58.695
I'm at school.

12:59.279 --> 13:00.489
It's all right. I can talk.

13:02.073 --> 13:04.493
That movie we saw? Of course, I remember.

13:05.619 --> 13:06.745
It's getting a sequel?

13:06.828 --> 13:08.288
Really?

13:10.665 --> 13:12.501
I guess it's that woman
from the other day.

13:14.961 --> 13:16.087
I haven't seen it.

13:16.171 --> 13:17.506
What's so funny?

13:30.644 --> 13:33.563
Shouldn't your top priorities
be studying and working on homework?

13:33.647 --> 13:34.481
Am I wrong?

13:38.235 --> 13:40.111
Why would he say that?
That came out of nowhere.

13:52.123 --> 13:55.210
He's never smiled at me like that.

13:59.172 --> 14:01.132
Is this what you call L-O-V-E?

14:02.842 --> 14:04.970
How have you managed
to endure this so many times?

14:05.887 --> 14:07.931
It's killing me.

14:08.557 --> 14:10.642
You learn from the pain and grow.

14:14.854 --> 14:16.481
I just wish it were all a novel.

14:18.066 --> 14:19.776
Then everything would be just as I wanted.

14:20.860 --> 14:23.238
From confessing my feelings
to the aftermath and the ending,

14:24.656 --> 14:26.491
everything would go just as I'd like then.

14:27.617 --> 14:29.911
So? Are you just going to give up?

14:31.955 --> 14:34.874
I haven't even started.
What is there to give up?

14:36.042 --> 14:37.586
What did I tell you?

14:37.669 --> 14:40.046
With L-O-V-E,
you just have to go straight for it.

14:41.256 --> 14:42.090
No.

14:44.884 --> 14:45.969
I won't.

14:48.346 --> 14:50.140
I'm done, Go-ya.

14:51.600 --> 14:53.018
If I keep going,

14:53.810 --> 14:55.562
I feel like I'll get hit by a bike

14:55.645 --> 14:58.815
and then by a car doing 140 kmph.

14:59.482 --> 15:01.109
I'll just end up a bloody mess.

15:04.154 --> 15:06.114
It's hard enough already.

15:08.325 --> 15:09.784
I'm just going to stop here.

15:13.663 --> 15:15.874
Mr. Ga sees her in a romantic light,

15:15.957 --> 15:17.083
but not me.

15:20.253 --> 15:22.505
That's not going to change
no matter what I do.

15:23.882 --> 15:25.550
Besides, more than anything,

15:26.676 --> 15:27.927
he looks happy.

15:30.305 --> 15:31.640
Isn't that what matters?

15:35.727 --> 15:36.728
You poor thing.

15:50.450 --> 15:52.118
This tastes amazing.

15:53.787 --> 15:55.830
Hey, where were you off to today?

15:57.207 --> 15:59.668
Did you go hang out
with your friend Deul-i?

16:00.251 --> 16:01.169
Don't be ridiculous.

16:01.252 --> 16:02.671
She's gone back to Seoul.

16:02.754 --> 16:04.089
No way.

16:05.131 --> 16:06.299
I can tell you met her.

16:07.300 --> 16:08.343
Are you two an item now,

16:08.843 --> 16:10.261
or is this a rekindled thing

16:10.929 --> 16:12.764
after breaking up back in the day?

16:12.847 --> 16:13.682
Just eat your dinner.

16:14.516 --> 16:15.517
He's changing the subject.

16:16.685 --> 16:18.228
What's wrong?

16:18.311 --> 16:19.229
Are you shy about it?

16:19.813 --> 16:21.189
Is that what's up, little Woo-su?

16:21.940 --> 16:23.066
So cute!

16:23.817 --> 16:26.236
He said he didn't, so give it a rest.

16:26.319 --> 16:27.320
Eat your dinner.

16:27.404 --> 16:28.947
Hey.

16:29.030 --> 16:30.949
Think about the countless women

16:31.032 --> 16:33.576
hooked by his looks
but turned off by his personality.

16:33.660 --> 16:34.536
Oh, those poor girls.

16:34.619 --> 16:35.954
-Tons of them.
-That's true.

16:36.996 --> 16:39.999
I've always been worried that
his long-term singleness would make him

16:40.083 --> 16:43.169
a toxic person who'd curse the world…

16:43.795 --> 16:44.671
Hey!

16:44.754 --> 16:45.880
-Dust.
-It doesn't hurt.

16:45.964 --> 16:46.881
I know all your moves.

16:46.965 --> 16:48.633
-Zero pain.
-You're still getting hit.

16:48.717 --> 16:50.552
-It doesn't hurt at all.
-Hey, we're eating here.

16:50.635 --> 16:52.137
-Are you kids, or what?
-No pain at all.

16:52.220 --> 16:53.304
-Jeez.
-You can't even dodge.

16:53.388 --> 16:54.973
-Guys.
-I'm landing twice as many hits!

16:57.976 --> 17:00.520
-Yoon's confession, what a twist!
-I never imagined Yoon would do that.

17:00.603 --> 17:02.147
Logically, it doesn't make sense,

17:02.230 --> 17:03.565
but emotionally, it's perfect.

17:04.315 --> 17:05.150
See?

17:05.233 --> 17:07.610
Everyone loves Yoon's confession.

17:07.694 --> 17:08.903
Why did he say it's weird?

17:16.536 --> 17:18.538
Does the writer go to Murim Girls' High?

17:25.295 --> 17:26.212
What the heck?

17:26.838 --> 17:28.006
What the heck is this?

17:28.506 --> 17:29.758
Is this someone from school?

17:30.842 --> 17:32.427
This must be just a lucky guess, right?

17:34.888 --> 17:36.973
Hands up if you're still up!

18:02.999 --> 18:05.794
DOES THE WRITER GO TO MURIM GIRLS' HIGH?

18:07.170 --> 18:08.505
Do you read web novels?

18:08.588 --> 18:10.799
Not recently.

18:10.882 --> 18:11.883
Why? Do you?

18:12.509 --> 18:14.052
No, not me.

18:14.135 --> 18:16.054
There's a web novel with main characters

18:16.596 --> 18:19.307
who are exactly like
the Korean literature, Math, PE,

18:19.390 --> 18:22.060
and Japanese teachers from our school.

18:22.143 --> 18:23.102
Huh? Really?

18:23.186 --> 18:24.437
Yeah.

18:24.521 --> 18:26.606
One of the main characters
is a math genius.

18:26.689 --> 18:29.484
Apparently, his personality
is just like Mr. Ga's.

18:30.151 --> 18:31.194
Isn't that weird?

18:31.277 --> 18:32.862
-No way.
-I know.

18:32.946 --> 18:35.448
I'm really curious who wrote it.

18:35.907 --> 18:38.701
If it were me,
I wouldn't be able to keep it a secret.

18:39.869 --> 18:41.329
Eui-ju, what do you think?

18:43.581 --> 18:44.541
About what?

18:45.250 --> 18:46.918
If it were you,
do you think you could hide it?

18:49.170 --> 18:50.129
Hide what?

18:52.966 --> 18:55.718
I was just asking.
Why are you getting so serious?

19:12.151 --> 19:13.111
So good.

19:13.903 --> 19:15.196
-Sexy food.
-Love the soup.

19:15.780 --> 19:16.739
Sexy food.

19:16.823 --> 19:19.075
She said it
like she had it all figured out.

19:20.326 --> 19:22.078
-This tastes great.
-Right?

19:22.871 --> 19:25.123
Did you hand in your math assignment?

19:26.749 --> 19:29.419
Should I ask her to keep it a secret?

19:30.044 --> 19:32.046
What if she tells
the whole school instead?

19:32.589 --> 19:33.965
No. What am I going to do?

19:36.634 --> 19:38.636
I asked if you've handed in
your math assignment.

19:38.720 --> 19:41.222
If you don't do it today,
you're bound to get more demerits.

19:41.306 --> 19:43.558
Right, I need to get on it.

19:43.641 --> 19:45.059
I'm going to do it later.

19:45.643 --> 19:46.477
Eui-ju.

19:46.561 --> 19:47.979
Don't forget, okay?

19:48.563 --> 19:49.397
Okay.

19:51.357 --> 19:52.734
What's wrong? Is everything okay?

19:53.693 --> 19:54.527
Yeah.

19:55.486 --> 19:57.238
The math thing is distracting her.

19:57.322 --> 19:59.157
The rolled omelet is amazing.

20:10.418 --> 20:12.837
One of the main characters
is a math genius.

20:12.921 --> 20:15.214
Apparently, his personality
is just like Mr. Ga's.

20:16.007 --> 20:17.008
Isn't that weird?

20:17.926 --> 20:19.218
Eui-ju, what do you think?

20:19.969 --> 20:22.263
If it were you,
do you think you could hide it?

20:22.847 --> 20:25.642
What if the whole school knows
by tomorrow?

20:41.658 --> 20:44.118
CHAPTER 41:
NOTHING STAYS A SECRET FOREVER

20:44.202 --> 20:45.536
-Hey, come here!
-She's sleeping again.

20:45.620 --> 20:47.330
Hey, where have you been?

20:47.413 --> 20:49.290
-Where did you go?
-Did you hit the snack bar?

20:50.208 --> 20:52.085
-We won't take no for an answer.
-Hand it over.

20:56.422 --> 20:58.132
-Hello.
-Hello.

21:02.261 --> 21:04.806
All right. Today is our first lesson
on "Gongmudohaga."

21:04.889 --> 21:06.432
Turn to page 168.

21:07.600 --> 21:08.893
Mr. Yoon.

21:09.560 --> 21:10.770
Yes?

21:10.853 --> 21:12.438
Is she going to expose me in class?

21:13.398 --> 21:14.816
She won't, right?

21:14.899 --> 21:16.943
Is this poem the last work
covered on the exam?

21:17.026 --> 21:18.194
Yes, that's right.

21:23.825 --> 21:24.742
Are you okay?

21:25.493 --> 21:26.703
Something's up, isn't it?

21:27.453 --> 21:28.538
It's nothing.

21:29.831 --> 21:31.958
"My beloved, don't cross that river."

21:32.583 --> 21:35.086
"Alas, you crossed the river."

21:35.795 --> 21:36.754
Should I

21:37.714 --> 21:39.465
just confess everything?

21:40.049 --> 21:44.262
Isn't that better than waiting nervously
for the other shoe to drop?

21:47.015 --> 21:48.266
Or should I just…

21:50.268 --> 21:53.896
DO YOU WANT TO DELETE THIS NOVEL?

22:36.105 --> 22:37.273
No way.

22:55.124 --> 22:56.125
Hey, Eui-ju.

22:56.209 --> 22:59.670
On my way to the art academy yesterday,
I snapped this photo of a cat.

22:59.754 --> 23:00.963
Isn't it cute?

23:04.383 --> 23:05.885
Is something wrong?

23:06.594 --> 23:07.929
Not at all.

23:15.436 --> 23:16.604
SPECIAL OFFER FOR THE INTERNET

23:21.109 --> 23:22.276
-Hey.
-Gosh.

23:23.069 --> 23:24.612
You're acting really weird.

23:24.695 --> 23:25.696
What's going on?

23:26.322 --> 23:27.990
I said it's nothing, didn't I?

23:33.496 --> 23:35.373
Sorry, I was just surprised.

23:37.834 --> 23:39.669
Oh, okay.

23:44.590 --> 23:47.135
So, f(x) equals the integral of…

23:48.344 --> 23:51.013
X plus three x squared.

23:51.722 --> 23:52.849
Then, the x cubed.

23:54.433 --> 23:55.726
This equals negative ten.

23:56.727 --> 23:58.646
So, put negative one into the formula,

23:58.729 --> 24:00.940
and you get negative ten.
Not too difficult, right?

24:01.023 --> 24:02.275
-No, sir.
-No, sir.

24:02.358 --> 24:03.442
Let's stop here for today.

24:03.526 --> 24:04.569
Great job.

24:04.652 --> 24:06.404
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

24:08.698 --> 24:10.825
-Goodbye.
-Goodbye.

24:19.458 --> 24:21.294
Mr. Ga, can I ask you a question?

24:23.045 --> 24:27.383
For number 356, I get that C is six,
but I'm not sure where to go from there.

24:28.134 --> 24:29.427
I'm sure you've got this.

24:29.510 --> 24:30.720
It's just a bit confusing.

24:32.054 --> 24:35.224
If you integrate here,
g(x) equals x cubed plus four, right?

24:36.017 --> 24:38.644
So you just need to find the value
when g is negative two.

24:39.562 --> 24:43.107
Always remember
that we can use the Product Rule this way.

24:43.191 --> 24:44.525
-Okay.
-Good job today.

24:45.026 --> 24:45.860
Mr. Ga.

24:49.071 --> 24:50.990
I brought this for you.

24:53.826 --> 24:55.203
You really didn't have to.

24:58.539 --> 24:59.665
Please don't do so again.

25:00.291 --> 25:01.542
Okay.

25:06.088 --> 25:08.132
-No difficulties following the class?
-Not yet.

25:08.841 --> 25:09.884
All right, then.

25:14.055 --> 25:15.139
Why are you still here?

25:16.599 --> 25:19.143
-Well…
-I guess you need to talk to Mr. Ga.

25:19.227 --> 25:21.270
If it's a question,
you could've asked in class.

25:26.901 --> 25:29.028
-I'll leave you to it.
-Okay.

25:38.246 --> 25:39.330
What is it?

25:42.959 --> 25:44.543
Mr. Ga, I really think

25:45.753 --> 25:48.756
I should take a break
from writing my web novel.

25:50.675 --> 25:51.509
Why?

25:52.802 --> 25:53.636
Well,

25:54.262 --> 25:56.138
I should focus on studying.

25:56.806 --> 25:59.684
Also, I keep forgetting to do my homework.

26:23.791 --> 26:25.876
Why have you lost confidence?
That's not like you.

26:26.711 --> 26:27.962
It's not like that.

26:28.587 --> 26:29.505
It's just…

26:30.047 --> 26:32.258
I thought a short break would do me good.

26:34.093 --> 26:36.429
I don't know what gave you that idea,

26:37.096 --> 26:39.056
but think back
on when you first started writing.

26:40.182 --> 26:42.893
Look back on why you started writing
this novel in the first place

26:42.977 --> 26:44.562
and how you felt then.

26:46.814 --> 26:48.232
That's where you'll find the answer

26:49.025 --> 26:52.111
on whether you really need a break,
or if that's just an excuse.

26:56.449 --> 26:57.908
You said you would keep at it

26:58.701 --> 26:59.869
and get better.

27:00.995 --> 27:02.330
Isn't that why you started?

27:04.915 --> 27:07.335
I'm not sure if I'm doing the right thing.

27:08.753 --> 27:12.131
Still, you've put my mind at ease, sir.

27:17.136 --> 27:18.220
Drink this and cheer up.

28:48.727 --> 28:50.729
Subtitle: Paul Carver
